WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.058
One customer portal, built three times, on three runtimes.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.667
Meet Azadi: the finance portal of an imaginary car maker.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:16.221
Customers sign in without a password. Date of birth, postcode and agreement number are enough.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:26.717
My account shows the agreement at a glance: the balance, the rate, the next payment, and how many are left.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.909
Paying takes one short form. Card details go straight to Stripe, not through the portal.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:46.946
From the same menu, customers can move their payment date, once per agreement, get a settlement figure, or order a paper statement.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.017
New bank details need three confirmations, and they're encrypted before they're stored.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.462
Contact details edit in place. Documents are a tap away.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:10.243
Then the portal was built three times: same pages, same templates, same data.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:17.000
Only the runtime changed. Spring Boot on a full JDK: 441 MB.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:24.179
Trimmed: 265. Helidon: about 150, first page in 1.3 seconds.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:27.527
Every release passes a health check before it takes traffic.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:32.554
Try the live demo at azadi-go.junaid.guru.
